<title>GREECE: Bank/Greece soaks 250 bln drs at 11.9pct in tender.</title>
<headline>Bank/Greece soaks 250 bln drs at 11.9pct in tender.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Greece drained 250 billion drachmas of 14-day funds at 11.90 percent in today's money tender, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The fixed rate tender was oversubscribed, it added.</p>
<p>&quot;Individual bids were thus satisfied pro rata on the basis of the ensuing allotment ratio of 15.71 percent.</p>
<p>A 14-day depo pact for 250 billion drachmas expires today, so liquidity is virtually unchanged.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
